	  Download-stream layout, GENERATED by tools/gen_mra.py from
	  ROM_START(cybrcomm) in src/mame/namco/namcos22.cpp (MAME 0.287).
	  Stream layout = the hardware-proven Ridge Racer.mra (System 22).

	    0x0000000   2.00M  maincpu     68020 program, 32-bit BE interleave
	    0x0200000   0.50M  sounddata   C74 external SEQ/data ROM (128K file repeated to fill the slot, as MAME ROM_RELOAD)
	    0x0280000   0.02M  c74         C74 internal mask ROM (namcoc74)
	    0x0284000   0.01M  c71         C71 DSP internal ROM (namcoc71)
	    0x0286000   2.00M  pointL      3D models plane L (1 MB used)
	    0x0486000   2.00M  pointM      3D models plane M (1 MB used)
	    0x0686000   2.00M  pointU      3D models plane U (1 MB used)
	    0x0886000  16.00M  textile     texture tiles (region bytes 0x800000+, tiles 0x8000-0xFFFF; core rebases, config 01)
	    0x1886000   2.00M  ccrl        texture tilemap LO
	    0x1A86000   0.50M  ccrh        texture tilemap ATTR
	    0x1B06000   4.00M  c352        samples (true region offsets, gaps padded, tail truncated)

	  Twin-stick tank game (two analog sticks in MAME); the core's driving inputs do not map it yet.
	  No hardware run yet: the core's per-game SDRAM map/config was only exercised with
	  Ridge Racer and Rave Racer; other S22 titles may need core-side follow-up.
	  gamma PROMs (rr1gam.*) omitted - gamma LUT is internal to the core.
	  Stream slots are FIXED (sys22_top.sv romload): point planes 0x286000/0x486000/0x686000,
	  textile 0x886000, ccrl 0x1886000, ccrh 0x1A86000, wave 0x1B06000; total 0x1F06000.
	  Factory EEPROM image from the romset on download index 8.
